  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1140 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nHave been monitoring the heavy rain and strong/severe\nthunderstorms just south of the CWA this evening. Very little\nconvection was found in the 402 area code early this evening and\nwe've been dry for a few hours now as the action is now entirely\nalong the front draped across Kansas and Missouri. Earlier\nNebraska action was in the vicinity of an 850mb front. \n\nFlooding has been reported in northeast Kansas as moisture \nstreams in from the Pacific as Hurricane Simon continues to spin\njust west of Sinaloa, MX. With a 995dam ridge spinning over the\nGulf of America and a 555dam upper low cut off over the Vegas \narea, strong southwest flow has pointed that source of \nsignificant moisture directly at the mid-Missouri River valley.\n\nThe front south of here will remain south of here overnight, so\nhave removed all but minimal PoPs along the southern state\nlines.",
